{
    "test_name": "MOB.531_AssetVerify_Asset_Search",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.531_AssetVerify_Asset_Search",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.531` The **asset search inside a mobile job** (`Job.tsx`, `Find Asset(s)`) \u2014 a\n`SearchInput` nothing was proving.\n- **Matched pair**: `Tank 0000` matches one of the fixture's two assets, so the other must\n  disappear; a nonsense term must empty the list; clearing must bring both back. The\n  negative leg is the test \u2014 a box that ignores its input still shows the row you wanted.\n- The fixture job has **exactly two assets**, which is what makes the middle assertion\n  meaningful: filtering to one PROVES exclusion, not just inclusion.\n- Reached with `av_job_gate` \u2014 the detail route is `cache-only` and renders blank if\n  deep-linked (never hand-roll a shorter gate).\n- **READ-ONLY** and self-restoring: it clears the box it typed into.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Asset Verification",
            "Search",
            "read-only"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
        "config": {
            "assertions": [],
            "config_variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "headers": {},
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{ MOBDEV }}"
            },
            "variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
